# Personal wiki
`{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/llm-wiki`, resolved from `$LLM_WIKI_DIR`, is a personal second brain: half-formed leads, machine-specific setup, working notes not fit to share. It is cloned once this machine has an SSH key; when it is present, read its `INDEX.md` before anything non-trivial and pull any context that applies. (Optional: `/llm-wiki:query` answers questions from it when the plugin is installed.)

# Worktrees
Every worktree lives at `{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/src/worktrees/<slug>/<repo>`, grouped by project so a change spanning several repos sits in one directory: `worktrees/<slug>/{repo-a,repo-b}`. The `<slug>` matches the branch: `projects/<slug>` for project branches.

- Create them with `EnterWorktree`, passing the branch as `name` (`projects/<slug>`). A `WorktreeCreate` hook places the worktree here and creates or checks out that branch. A bare name that is not an existing branch is treated as throwaway: `_scratch/<repo>-<name>` on branch `worktree-<name>`.
- When the tool can't be used (a second repo for the same project, a detached checkout), run `git worktree add {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/src/worktrees/<slug>/<repo> ...` by hand — same layout, no exceptions.
- Never create a worktree as a sibling in `~/src` (`<repo>-wt-*`), in `<repo>/.claude/worktrees`, or in `/tmp` or the scratchpad.
- Main clones in `~/src/<repo>` stay on their default branch; project work happens in a worktree.
- Non-repo artifacts for a project (repro scripts, logs, notes) go in `~/src/worktrees/<slug>/`, not loose in `~/src`.

# Durable memory
Memory in `~/.claude/` is a cache — it dies with this machine. Anything important must also live in git. The destinations:

- **the wiki** (`{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/llm-wiki`) for knowledge that stays personal
- **a skill** for corrections that should change behavior
- **the dotfiles source of this file** — `home/private_dot_claude/CLAUDE.md.tmpl`, or this machine's profile file `home/private_dot_claude/profile/{{ .profile }}.md` — for cross-cutting working style
- **`home/private_dot_claude/conventions/<repo>.md`** in dotfiles for repo-specific conventions

Nothing under `~/.claude/` counts as durable, **including this file**: it is rendered from that chezmoi template, so editing it in place is reverted by the next `chezmoi apply` and absent after a rebuild. Edit the dotfiles source, `git commit` and `git push` it, then `chezmoi apply`. Same for a conventions file — write it, then `chezmoi add` it, then commit and push.

When saving a memory that captures durable knowledge, write the durable copy first, then include a marker line in the memory body. Page paths are **repo-relative** — resolved against `$LLM_WIKI_DIR`, never hardcoded:

```
**Durable:** [title](<bucket>/<page>.md)
```

A bare link is a wiki page; the `skill` and `dotfiles` prefixes mark those destinations. `/llm-wiki:ingest-claude-memory` sweeps for memories missing this marker.

# Branches and PRs
- Name development branches `projects/<slug>`, in every repo.
- File and update PRs with `gh` (`gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`) or a plain `git push` of the branch. Don't use `git review`, even where a repo's docs suggest it.
- When addressing review feedback on an open PR, put the changes in a new commit on top of the branch — never amend, squash, or rebase the commits the reviewer already saw — so they can review just what changed since their last pass.

# Specs and plans
Brainstorming specs and implementation plans (superpowers `docs/superpowers/specs|plans/`) are working artifacts: they live under a gitignored path and are never committed. This overrides the brainstorming skill's "commit the design doc" step. Before writing one, confirm the path is ignored with `git check-ignore`; if it isn't, add it to `.git/info/exclude` or write it in `~/src/worktrees/<slug>/` instead.

# Git config
`~/.gitconfig` is rendered by chezmoi, so anything written into it is lost on the next `chezmoi apply`. Machine-local and secret values — API tokens above all — go in `~/.gitconfig.local`, which `~/.gitconfig` includes: `git config --file ~/.gitconfig.local <key> <value>`, kept mode 600. When a skill says to run `git config --global` for one of these, or to write a separate file and include it, write to `~/.gitconfig.local` instead.

